  <!--CVE-2026-42154 is a missing length check on the /api/v1/read remote-read endpoint of Prometheus
      THE SERVER (Go, github.com/prometheus/prometheus, fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3). This service ships
      the Java client library instead - github.com/prometheus/client_java, as
      io.prometheus:prometheus-metrics-* 1.7.0 via micrometer-registry-prometheus. It exposes a scrape
      endpoint and implements no remote-read API, so the vulnerable code path does not exist here.
      Different project, different language, no shared code: dependency-check matches on the
      "prometheus" product name, and our 1.7.0 falls inside the server's "< 3.5.3" range by coincidence.
      Re-check this if the service ever gains a real Prometheus server dependency.-->
  <suppress>
    <notes>CVE-2026-42154 affects the Prometheus server (Go), not the io.prometheus Java client</notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.prometheus/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-42154</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>CVE-2026-42154 affects the Prometheus server (Go), not micrometer's Prometheus registry</notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.micrometer/micrometer\-registry\-prometheus@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-42154</cve>
  </suppress>
